[size=5][b]SailingTogether — cooperative rowing[/b][/size]

In vanilla Valheim only the player at the helm can move the ship. With [b]SailingTogether[/b], every player [b]sitting on a ship bench[/b] can row with [b]W[/b] (forward) and [b]S[/b] (backward) instead of standing up. [b]Jump[/b] still stands you up.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]BepInEx is required[/b] — install [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/denikson/BepInExPack_Valheim/]BepInExPack Valheim[/url] (5.4.x) before this mod.
[*][b]Every player on the ship must have the mod installed.[/b]
[/list]

[size=4][b]How it works[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Rowing works at [b]speed 1 (oars)[/b] and in reverse. Optionally also while stopped ([i]RowInStop[/i]), which allows rowing with nobody at the helm.
[*]Each rower pushes on the side of the ship they are sitting on:
[/list]
[code]
 Left | Right | Result
------+-------+----------------------------
  W   |   W   | straight, faster
  W   |   -   | turns right
  -   |   W   | turns left
  W   |   S   | spins in place to the right
  S   |   S   | brakes / goes backward
[/code]
[list]
[*]The helmsman keeps full control of speed and rudder; the rowers' force is added on top.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Ship HUD[/b][/size]
A top-down view of the ship, built from the game's own icons:
[list]
[*][b]Helmsman:[/b] every bench, who is sitting, and each rower's direction.
[*][b]Rower:[/b] only your own bench and your rowing direction.
[*]Animated oars that sway like the vanilla helm oar, and green/red arrows outside the hull.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] install the main file with Vortex.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into the Valheim folder. It contains [i]BepInEx/plugins/SailingTogether/SailingTogether.dll[/i].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
[i]BepInEx/config/farias.SailingTogether.cfg[/i] (created on first run): rowing power, turn rate, center dead zone, rowing while stopped / in reverse, HUD scale and position, and an optional debug simulator (F8, disabled by default) for testing alone.

